see "../src/rng.vox".
see "../src/gen_literals.vox".
see "../src/gen_manifest.vox".
see "../src/gen_core.vox".
see "../src/gen_buffers.vox".
see "../src/gen_files.vox".
see "../src/gen_collections.vox".
see "../src/gen_text.vox".
see "../src/gen_things.vox".
see "../src/gen_flow.vox".
see "../src/gen_misc.vox".
see "../src/gen_process.vox".
see "../src/gen_expressions.vox".
see "../src/gen_keywords.vox".
see "../src/gen_basics.vox".

(The ledger's buffer leaves, batch A - docs/ledger/buffers.md rows
 BUF-01, BUF-03, BUF-05, BUF-07, BUF-10, BUF-11, BUF-12, BUF-13.

 Each leaf is called directly off a pinned rng seed and its emitted
 source printed in full, so the golden is the generated Vox itself. That
 is the point: these leaves exist to emit assertions, and an assertion
 whose text drifts is an assertion nobody is reading. A diff here is
 either a deliberate change to what a claim is put on trial with, or a
 bug in the rendering - and the second kind is what caught the first
 version of the assertion line, whose trailing `Otherwise` silently
 swallowed every statement that followed it.

 Each leaf is emitted twice, at the true top level (nested false, every
 line closed by its own period) and inside a block (nested true, every
 line but the last continued by a comma). Those are the two ways 'gen
 join lines' can render a line and they are not interchangeable - the
 nested rendering is the one the bug above only showed up in.

 The name allocator is exercised on its own at the end: the whole
 vocabulary, never twice in one program, and a suffix only once the
 words run out.)

(The buffer leaves that write a file interpolate the scratch flag's
 name, which a live program gets from its manifest. This test drives the
 leaves directly rather than through 'gen program', so it names one
 itself.)
Set gen_scratch_flag to "'the workspace'".
Set gen_does_file_io to true.

Print "--- BUF-01, BUF-05: declaration forms and exact capacity ---".
'rng seed' of 11.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer declaration' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 11.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer declaration' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- BUF-10, BUF-11, BUF-12: size, length, capacity, empty ---".
'rng seed' of 23.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer properties' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 23.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer properties' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- BUF-13: full, filled to capacity exactly ---".
'rng seed' of 5.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer fullness' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- BUF-13 again, a different split and a dynamic buffer ---".
'rng seed' of 91.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer fullness' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- BUF-03: dynamic growth past the reserve ---".
'rng seed' of 3.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer growth' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- BUF-07: a read that truncates, detected by size ---".
'rng seed' of 47.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer truncation' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

(A program that never committed to file I/O was never given a path, so
 the truncation leaf must not invent one - it stands aside for a leaf
 that needs nothing but memory.)
Print "--- BUF-07 with no file I/O committed ---".
Set gen_does_file_io to false.
'rng seed' of 47.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf buffer truncation' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
Print "emits a property assertion instead: {'gen text contains' of \"ASSERT BUF-1\"}".
Set gen_does_file_io to true.

Print "--- names: the whole vocabulary, no repeats, suffix only after that ---".
'rng seed' of 8.
'gen buffer names reset'.
a number called 'the names taken' is 0.
a text called 'the roll call' is "".
While 'the names taken' is less than 33,
    a text called 'the stem' is 'gen buffer name',
    a text called 'the name' is 'gen buffer reference' of 'the stem',
    Set 'the roll call' to "{'the roll call'}{'the name'} ",
    Set 'the names taken' to 'the names taken' add 1.
Print 'the roll call'.
Print "a fresh program starts the vocabulary over: ".
'gen buffer names reset'.
a text called 'the fresh stem' is 'gen buffer name'.
Print 'gen buffer property' of 'the fresh stem' and "capacity".
